  <content>
  <section><title> Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>
<para>Just as polynomials can be added and subtracted, polynomial functions can also be added and subtracted.</para>

<note>
  <para><emphasis>For functions \(f(x)\) and \(g(x)\),</emphasis></para>
  <hr/>
  <list>
    <item>\((f + g)(x) = f(x) + g(x)\)</item>
    <item>\((f - g)(x) = f(x) - g(x)\)</item>
  </list>
</note>

<para>Let’s look at some examples.</para>
<para>For the functions \(f(x) = 3x^2-5x+7\) and \(g(x) = x^2-4x-3\), find:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((f+g)(x)\) </item>
  <item>\(
    (f+g)(3)
    \)</item>
  <item>\(
    (f-g)(x)
    \)</item>
  <item>\(
    (f-g)(-2)
    \)</item>
</list>
<para>The following is a step-by-step breakdown.
</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>(\(f+g)(x)=f(x)+g(x)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - 
  </emphasis>Substitute </para>
<para>\(f(x)={\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7}\) and \(g(x)={\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3}\).
  \((f+g)(x)=({\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7})+{\style{color:blue}(}{\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3}{\style{color:blue})}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Rewrite without the parentheses.</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=3x^2-5x+7-x^2-4x-3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Put like terms together.</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=3x^2+x^2-5x-4x+7-3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Combine like terms.</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=4x^2-9x+4\)</para>
<para>In part (a), we found \((f+g)(x)\), and now are asked to find \((f+g)(3)\).</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f+g)(x)=4x^2-9x+4\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> To find \((f+g)(3)\), substitute \(x=3\).</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(3)=4(3)^2-9 \cdot 3+4\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Simplify. </para>
<para>  \((f+g)(3)=4 \cdot 9-9 \cdot 3+ 4\)
  \((f+g)(3)=36-27+4\)
  \((f+g)(3)=13\)</para>
<para>Notice that we could have found \((f+g)(3)\) by first finding the values of \(f(3)\) and \(g(3)\) separately and then adding the results.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Find \(f (3)\).</para>
<para>  \(f(x)=3x^2-5x+7\)
  \( f({\style{color:red}3})=3({\style{color:red}3})^2-5({\style{color:red}3})+7\)
  \(f(3)=19\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Find \(g(3)\).</para>
<para>  \(g(x)=x^2-4x-3\)
  \(g(3)=-6\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Find \((f+g)(3)\).</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=f(x)+g(x)\)
  \((f+g)(3)=f(3)+g(3)\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Substitute \(f(3)={\style{color:red}1}{\style{color:red}9}\) and \(g(3)= {\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}6}\).</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(3)=19+(-6)\)
  \((f+g)(3)=13\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f-g)(x)=f(x)-g(x)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - 
  </emphasis>Substitute </para>
<para>\(f(x)={\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7}\) and \(g(x)= {\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3}\).
  \((f-g)(x)=( {\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7})-({\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3})\) </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Rewrite without the parentheses.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(x)=3x^2-5x+7-x^2+4x+3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Put like terms together.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(x)=3x^2-x^2-5x+4x+7+3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 - 
  </emphasis>Combine like terms.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(x)=2x^2-x+10\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f-g)(x)=2x^2-x+10\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> To find \((f-g)(-2)\), substitute \(x={\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2}\).</para>
<para>  \((f-g)( {\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})=2({\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})^2-({\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})+10\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Simplify.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(-2)=2 \cdot 5-(-2)+10\)
  \((f-g)(-2)=20\)</para>

<title> Try It: Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>For functions \(f(x)=2x^2-4x+3\) and \(g(x)=x^2-2x-6\), find:</para>
    <para>\((f+g)(x)\)</para>
      <para>\((f+g)(3)\)</para>
      <para>\((f-g)(x)\)</para>
      <para>\((f-g)(-2)\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Here is how to add and subtract the polynomial functions:</para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f+g)(x)&amp;=&amp;(2x^2-4x+3)+(x^2-2x-6)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^2-4x+3+x^2-2x-6\\&amp;=&amp;3x^2-6x-3\end{array}\)
      
    </item>
    <item> \(\begin{array}{rcl}(f+g)(3)&amp;=&amp;3(3)^2-6(3)-3\\&amp;=&amp;3(9)-6(3)-3\\&amp;=&amp;27-18-3\\&amp;=&amp;6\end{array}\)
    </item>
    <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f-g)(x)&amp;=&amp;(2x^2-4x+3)-(x^2-2x-6)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^2-4x+3-x^2+2x+6\\&amp;=&amp;x^2-2x+9\;\end{array}\)
      
    </item>
    <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f-g)(-2)&amp;=&amp;(-2)^2-2(-2)+9\;\\&amp;=&amp;(4)+4+9\;\\&amp;=&amp;17\;\end{array}\)</item>
  </list>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
